sweet ufs: one PRDT entry per 4 KiB page

The Exynos UFSHCI on stallion transfers only the first 4 KiB of a larger
PRDT entry (a 2-block GPT entry-array read returned block 1 only, so
"super" and "userdata", entries 33/34, were invisible). Linux always
hands the host page-sized segments; do the same. 1 MiB / 4 KiB = 256
entries = 5 KiB of UCD, which fits the 12 KiB slot before DMA_BOUNCE.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -71,7 +71,12 @@
 
 #define UFS_BLOCK       4096u
 #define BOUNCE_SIZE     (1u << 20)
-#define PRDT_CHUNK      (256u << 10)            /* PRDT byte count field: 18 bits */
+/*
+ * One PRDT entry per 4 KiB page, as Linux's scatterlists always give the
+ * host: the Exynos UFSHCI (stallion) moves only the first 4 KiB of a
+ * larger entry (a 2-block GPT read returned the first block only).
+ */
+#define PRDT_CHUNK      4096u
 #define PRDT_MAX        (BOUNCE_SIZE / PRDT_CHUNK)
 #define CMD_TIMEOUT_NS  (5ull * NSEC_PER_SEC)
 #define CMD_SPIN_NS     (50ull * NSEC_PER_USEC)
